---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';

import roofLiningImage from '@/assets/car-roof-lining-repair/roof-lining.jpg';
import processShapeImage from '@/assets/car-roof-lining-repair/process-shape.jpg';
import processCutImage from '@/assets/car-roof-lining-repair/process-cut.jpg';
import roofRestoreImage from '@/assets/car-roof-lining-repair/roof-restore.jpg';
import beforeAfterToyotaPriusImage from '@/assets/car-roof-lining-repair/before-after-toyota-prius.png';
import sunroofImage from '@/assets/car-roof-lining-repair/sunroof.png';
---

<BaseLayout>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>Car Roof Lining Repair and Restoration in Singapore | Five Star Auto Leather</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Sagging car roof lining? We restore roof liners, headliners & upholstery for all makes and models in Singapore. Book your slot today."
    />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="order-2 sm:order-1">
      <Image
        src={roofLiningImage}
        alt="Technician performing car roof lining repair in Singapore"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="h-full w-full bg-black object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="order-1 flex items-center justify-center bg-black px-4 py-8 sm:order-2 sm:px-16">
      <div
        class="title-slide-up flex h-full flex-col items-center justify-center text-center text-white sm:items-start sm:text-left"
      >
        <h1 class="text-4xl">Professional Car Roof Lining Repair and Restoration in Singapore</h1>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Is your car roof lining sagging, stained, or peeling? Five Star Auto Leather restores car
          roof linings to a factory-quality finish with premium materials tailored to your vehicle.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/contact-us"
          class="mt-8 inline-block w-36 rounded bg-red-700 px-4 py-2 text-center text-sm font-medium transition-colors hover:bg-red-600"
        >
          Get in Touch
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-7xl flex-col items-center gap-8 px-4 py-8 sm:px-6">
    <div class="text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl">The Problem: Why Roof Linings Sag</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Most factory roof linings use a foam-backed fabric that degrades over time, especially in
        Singapore's heat and humidity. Common signs include:
      </p>
    </div>

    <table class="w-full border-collapse border border-gray-300">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-gray-100">
          <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3 text-left">Symptom</th>
          <th class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3 text-left">Cause</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Fabric drooping at the edges</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Adhesive breakdown from heat exposure</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Bubbling or rippling</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Moisture trapped between foam and fabric</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Visible stains or yellowing</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Age, wear and tear, and sun damage</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3">Foam crumbling when touched</td>
          <td class="border border-gray-300 px-4 py-3"
            >Foam degradation (common in cars 5+ years old)</td
          >
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="text-center">
      Good news: All cases are fixable. We assess, quote, and restore most jobs usually within the
      same day.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto grid max-w-7xl grid-cols-1 px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-12">
    <div class="mx-auto aspect-9/16 w-full max-w-[300px] overflow-hidden lg:col-span-4">
      <iframe
        src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/video.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Freel%2F1009400853873591&show_text=false"
        title="Roof Lining Restoration Process"
        frameborder="0"
        allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
        allowfullscreen
        loading="lazy"
        class="h-full w-full rounded-lg shadow-lg"></iframe>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6 ml-0 flex flex-col justify-center lg:col-span-8 lg:mt-0 lg:ml-6">
      <h2 class="mb-2 text-center text-2xl lg:text-left">Our Roof Lining Restoration Process</h2>
      <p class="mb-8 text-center lg:text-left">
        See how the restoration is done in our workshop. Watch our roof lining restoration process.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 1: Free Assessment & Quote</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Bring your vehicle to our workshop or simply send us your car's make and model. As every
        vehicle is different, from compact hatchbacks to SUVs and MPVs, we provide a tailored
        quotation based on your vehicle and material selection.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 2: Removal & Preparation</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        We carefully remove the existing roof liner, strip away the old deteriorated foam and
        adhesive, then prepare the backing board so the new material bonds strongly and lasts.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 3: Precision Bonding</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Using premium, high-temperature industrial adhesives (formaldehyde-free and proven for
        Singapore's tropical climate), we bond the new headliner fabric for a smooth, wrinkle-free
        finish with no bubbles or sagging.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Step 4: Reinstallation & Quality Check</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        We reinstall the restored roof liner and refit all trim pieces, grab handles, lights and sun
        visors with care. Every installation undergoes a final inspection for fit, alignment and
        finish before your vehicle is returned.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="col-span-full mt-8 grid w-full grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <Image
        src={processShapeImage}
        alt="Technician smoothing fresh headliner fabric onto a moulded panel during car roof lining repair"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="h-full w-full rounded-lg bg-black object-cover"
      />
      <Image
        src={processCutImage}
        alt="Technician trimming openings from the back of the moulded roof board during car headliner repair"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="h-full w-full rounded-lg bg-black object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bg-black">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-7xl flex-col gap-8 px-4 py-8 text-white sm:px-6">
      <div class="text-center">
        <h2 class="text-2xl">Vehicles We Service</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">We restore roof linings for all vehicle makes and models, including:</p>
      </div>

      <ul class="mx-auto space-y-2">
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
          <span>Hatchbacks and sedans</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
          <span>SUVs and MPVs</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
          <span>Luxury and continental cars</span>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
          <Icon name="mdi:checkbox-marked-circle-outline" class="h-4 w-4 shrink-0" />
          <span>Commercial vans and vehicles</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="text-center">Call us for a quick quote based on your car model.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="order-1 md:order-2">
      <Image
        src={roofRestoreImage}
        alt="Technician securing loose overhead wiring against the bare roof frame during car roof lining repair"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
        widths={[640, 1280]}
        sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
        class="h-full w-full bg-black object-cover"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="order-2 flex h-full flex-col justify-center px-4 py-8 md:order-1 md:px-16">
      <h2 class="mb-8 text-center text-2xl">Why Choose Five Star Auto Leather?</h2>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Transparent Pricing</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Every roof lining restoration is quoted based on your vehicle's roof size and your chosen
        material. No misleading "from" prices, no hidden charges. Just honest pricing tailored to
        your car.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Minimal Downtime, Maximum Convenience</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Most restorations are completed within a day. For added convenience, you can even drive your
        car after we remove the roof board and return the next day for reinstallation. This gives
        the adhesive time to fully cure while allowing any residual odour to dissipate, with
        dismantling and installation taking just 1–2 hours each.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">Built for Singapore's Climate</h3>
      <p class="mb-4">
        We use premium headliner materials and high-temperature, formaldehyde-free adhesives
        selected specifically for Singapore's heat and humidity, helping ensure your new roof lining
        stays secure for years to come.
      </p>
      <h3 class="mb-2 font-bold">100% In-House Craftsmanship</h3>
      <p>
        Every restoration is carried out by our experienced team at our Singapore workshop — never
        outsourced. From careful preparation to final installation, we maintain complete quality
        control and back our workmanship with a warranty for your peace of mind.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-7xl flex-col items-center gap-8 px-4 py-8 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-2xl">Before & After</h2>

    <!-- TODO: add more? 
    is this toyota -->
    <Image
      src={beforeAfterToyotaPriusImage}
      alt="Toyota Prius roof panel before and after car headliner repair"
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
      widths={[640, 1280]}
      sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 50vw"
      class="mx-auto max-w-2xl rounded-lg object-cover"
    />
  </section>

  <section class="bg-black">
    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-7xl flex-col gap-8 px-4 py-8 text-white sm:px-6">
      <h2 class="text-center text-2xl">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">
          What's the difference between a roof liner, roof lining, and headliner?
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          They're all different names for the same thing — the upholstered fabric covering the
          interior ceiling of your car. Whether you call it a roof liner, roof lining, or headliner,
          it's the same restoration service.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Can you match my original factory colour and texture?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We carry a wide range of headliner fabrics in different colours and textures to closely
          match your vehicle's original interior. While an exact factory match isn't always
          possible, we always recommend the closest available option.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">What if my car has a sunroof?</h3>
        <Image
          src={sunroofImage}
          alt="Car roof lining repair sunroof comparison"
          loading="lazy"
          widths={[300, 600]}
          sizes="(max-width: 384px) 100vw, 384px"
          class="mx-auto mt-4 w-full max-w-sm rounded-lg object-cover"
        />
        <p class="mt-4">
          No problem. We can restore the main roof lining on vehicles with sunroofs. If your sunroof
          has a removable hardboard panel, we can rewrap that too. However, if your vehicle has a
          panoramic roof with a retractable roller blind, the blind itself cannot be rewrapped due
          to its construction.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">How long does a roof lining restoration take?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Most roof lining restorations are completed within a day. To minimise your downtime, you
          also have the option to drive your car after we remove the roof board and return the
          following day for reinstallation. This allows the adhesive to cure properly and any
          residual odour to dissipate, while dismantling and installation each take only 1–2 hours.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Do I need to book an appointment?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Yes. We recommend booking an appointment so we can dedicate the necessary time to your
          vehicle. Walk-ins are welcome but are subject to workshop availability.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="font-bold">Do you provide a warranty?</h3>
        <p class="mt-4">
          Yes. We provide a 1-year workmanship warranty on all roof lining restorations, giving you
          added peace of mind. Feel free to ask us for the full warranty details during your visit.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <iframe
    src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3988.6660102489027!2d103.8690919!3d1.3770706000000001!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x31da1658b06d3b7d%3A0xbb4992fe537bc610!2sFive%20Star%20Auto%20Leather!5e0!3m2!1sen!2ssg!4v1766728446154!5m2!1sen!2ssg"
    width="100%"
    height="400"
    style="border:0;"
    allowfullscreen=""
    loading="lazy"
    referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"></iframe>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h2 {
    font-family: 'RacingSansOne', var(--font-sans);
  }
</style>
